<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Oct 9.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Oct 9.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Tuesday.</p>
<p>P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		    P/E	 Close</p>
<p> 1 Portman Min	     301.59    1.90</p>
<p> 2 Niugini Min	     280.58    3.90</p>
<p> 3 Mayne Nickless	  196.83    8.70</p>
<p> 4 T N T		     171.94    2.39</p>
<p> 5 Adel Bton Cement	121.74    1.68</p>
<p> 6 Colonial Coml	   118.03    2.16</p>
<p> 7 Herald Rsc		 89.38    1.01</p>
<p> 8 Forrestania Gold	 87.30    2.20</p>
<p> 9 Westral Forest	   76.09    2.10</p>
<p>10 Energy Equity	    67.69    0.88</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1 Dominion Min		2.77    0.67</p>
<p> 2 Computer Power	    3.35    3.43</p>
<p> 3 Premier Inv		 3.95    0.70</p>
<p> 4 Parbury Ltd		 5.88    0.69</p>
<p> 5 BTR Plc		     5.91    5.50</p>
<p> 6 Aust Gold Rsc	     6.58    1.20</p>
<p> 7 Pac Mutal Aust	    6.75    2.41</p>
<p> 8 McIntosh Sec		7.23    0.90</p>
<p> 9 OLS Asia Hldgs	    7.23    0.86</p>
<p>10 Capcount Prop	     7.87    0.86</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
